WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:10.375
The Hubble Space Telescope is a space telescope that was launched into low Earth orbit in 1990 during the STS-31 and remains in operation.

00:10.918 --> 00:20.296
It is regarded as one of the largest and most versatile space telescopes, renowned as a vital research tool and as a public relations boon for astronomy.

00:20.838 --> 00:27.253
The Hubble Space Telescope is named after astronomer Edwin Hubble and is one of NASA's Great Observatories.

00:27.886 --> 00:40.368
The Space Telescope Science Institute (STScI) selects Hubble's targets and processes the resulting data, while the Goddard Space Flight Center (GSFC) controls the spacecraft.
